cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  bsard2currentlawmatching: A Belgian Statutory Corpus
  Database for Retrieval-Augmented Generation
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using these
  metadata. Please also cite the underlying BSARD dataset
  (see DATA_LICENSE.md).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Marios
    family-names: Paschalidis
    email: paschalidismarios@gmail.com
    affiliation: KU Leuven
repository-code: "https://github.com/MariusPasch/bsard-rag-thesis"
abstract: >-
  Code and ETL pipeline that build a SQLite corpus database
  (with Parquet and JSONL exports) of every article from 49
  Justel consolidated Belgian law PDFs, linked to the Belgian
  Statutory Article Retrieval Dataset (BSARD) and enriched
  with structural hierarchy, citation-graph, and verification
  metadata. The corpus is the single source of truth for the
  downstream RAG retrieval experiments (RQ1-RQ3) of a master's
  thesis at KU Leuven.
keywords:
  - information retrieval
  - legal NLP
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - BSARD
  - corpus construction
  - Belgian law
license: MIT
